{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:02637bbd99d0264f","name":"Battle Hydra","source":{"id":"source:reference-02637bbd99d0264f","title":"Battle Hydra","revision":16168,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:25Z","sha256":"eae54a44f7063b817628d4e0922a233d92b055d702f2ced8db069cc8c0123680","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16168","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Battle%20Hydra&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-02637bbd99d0264f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Battle Hydras are the result of Sith Lord Exar Kun's experimentation with Sith Alchemy. Battle Hydras usually have two heads, although varieties with more than two heads are also possible. In addition to their multiple heads, Battle Hydras have leathery wings and a whiplike tail ending in a barbed stinger that drips with poison. The skin of a Battle Hydra is infused with ancient Sith alloys, granting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Battle Hydras spend most of their time aloft, riding thermal currents in search of prey or threats. When something is spotted, the Battle Hydra dives through the air, attacking with its teeth, claws, and poisoned stinger. Once prey succumbs to its attacks or poison, it scoops up the corpse and hauls it back to its lair, where it is torn apart and devoured.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Battle Hydras are susceptible to the commands of Force-sensitive darksiders, many of whom use Battle Hydras as their own personal shocktroopers.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Battle Hydra Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Battle Hydras are most commonly encountered on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin 4"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin_4","referenceId":"reference:5f008a1b1f754b64"},", where they prowl the skies above its steamy jungles. However, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exar Kun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exar_Kun","referenceId":"reference:ecc01bec6de14936"}," traveled far and wide, and it's possible that they might be found anywhere that has an abundant food supply. Battle Hydras are particularly attracted to sites closely connected to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", perhaps drawing some kind of sustenance from them. A Dark Side character looking to acquire a Battle Hydra minion usually seeks out these sinister places, knowing that Battle Hydras are likely to be found nearby.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Battle Hydra Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large Airborne ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +15; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 30 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 23), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 22, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 19 (Dual